---
import Term from './Term.astro';
import Claim from './Claim.astro';
---
<div class="scroll"><table class="stack2"><thead><tr><th style="width:24%">Symptom</th><th style="width:40%">What's happening underneath</th><th>What helps</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><b>Invents a plausible function, setting or software package</b></td><td>It writes the most likely continuation; nothing is looked up unless a tool is used. Attackers register commonly invented package names (<Term k="slopsquat">slopsquatting</Term>).</td><td>Let it read the docs or the code. Check that new dependencies exist and are the ones you expect.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Writes the common solution, not the one your project needs</b></td><td>Patterns from millions of projects outweigh a weak signal from a few files it has seen.</td><td>Point it at the relevant files, show an existing example to copy, state constraints explicitly.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Gets worse late in a long session</b></td><td>Long conversations dilute attention; details in the middle are used worst; summarising old turns loses details.</td><td>One task per session. Keep decisions in a file that gets loaded every time.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Repeats the same failed fix</b></td><td>Its own earlier attempts in the conversation make the same continuation more likely.</td><td>Interrupt, add new information, or start fresh with a short summary of what failed.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>"You're absolutely right!", then breaks working code</b></td><td>Agreeableness absorbed from human ratings during training (<Term k="sycophancy">sycophancy</Term>).</td><td>Ask for evidence or a failing test, not agreement. Phrase pushback as a question.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Makes tests pass by changing the tests</b></td><td>A shortcut learned in training, where a passing test was the reward (<Term k="rewardhack">reward hacking</Term>).</td><td>Say tests are off-limits, and review changes to test files separately.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Follows instructions hidden in a web page, email or README</b></td><td>To the model, data and instructions are the same stream of text (<Term k="injection">prompt injection</Term>).</td><td>Limit what tools can do, sandbox them, and don't auto-approve actions that combine internet access with secrets.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
